              "text": "To watch **MSNBC** live online, it is helpful to know that the network underwent a major rebranding. On November 15, 2025, MSNBC officially changed its name to **MS NOW** (which stands for *My Source for News, Opinion, and the World*) after spinning off from NBCUniversal to its new parent company, Versant. \n\nWhile there is no permanent, 100% free official live *video* stream of the 24/7 channel without a TV provider, you can legally watch or listen for free using several official methods:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Watch via Free Trials on Live TV Streaming Services\nYou can sign up for a free trial with a live TV streaming service that carries MS NOW. These trials typically last between 5 to 7 days, allowing you to watch the live television feed for free. Just make sure to cancel before the trial period ends if you do not want to be charged.\n*   **Fubo:** Offers a free trial and carries the live MS NOW feed.\n*   **DirecTV Stream:** Often offers free trials and is one of the most reliable ways to stream MS NOW live.\n*   **YouTube TV:** Frequently provides free trials for new users and includes MS NOW in its base package.\n\n### 2. Log In with an Existing TV Provider\nIf you, a family member, or a friend has a traditional cable, satellite, or live TV streaming subscription (like Hulu + Live TV, Sling TV, or YouTube TV), you can stream the channel for free:\n*   Go to **[msnbc.com](https://www.msnbc.com)** (which redirects to the official **ms.now** domain) or download the **MS NOW app** on your phone, tablet, or smart TV.\n*   Select \"Live TV\" and sign in using your TV provider credentials for unlimited, high-definition live streaming.\n\n### 3. Stream the Live Audio Feed (100% Free & Legal)\nIf you do not need the video and just want to listen to the live, real-time broadcast of shows like *Morning Joe*, *The Rachel Maddow Show*, or *The Beat with Ari Melber*, you can stream the audio 24/7 completely for free:\n*   **The MS NOW App:** Download the official MS NOW app on iOS or Android; it features a free live-audio stream of the network's broadcast.\n*   **TuneIn Radio:** Search for \"MS NOW\" (or MSNBC) on the free TuneIn app or website to stream the live radio simulcast.\n*   **SiriusXM:** If you have a SiriusXM subscription (or are using a free trial), you can listen to the live broadcast on Channel 118.\n\n### 4. Watch Free On-Demand Video Clips\nIf you missed a show and want to catch up on the most important segments, monologues, and interviews for free:\n*   **YouTube:** The official **[MS NOW YouTube Channel](https://www.youtube.com/@msnow)** is updated constantly throughout the day with free, high-quality segments of all major prime-time and daytime programs shortly after they air.\n*   **Official Website/App:** You can watch a rotating selection of recent news clips and highlights directly on the MS NOW app or website without needing to sign in with a TV provider.",
